WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:02.635 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Congratulations on
the success of the show.

00:00:02.635 --> 00:00:04.104
We had Chrissy Metz --
Your co-star was here last week.

00:00:04.104 --> 00:00:05.105 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Love her.

00:00:05.105 --> 00:00:06.539 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we were just
talking about --

00:00:06.539 --> 00:00:08.074 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I wonder
what it´s like for you.

00:00:08.074 --> 00:00:10.110 align:start size:94% position:6%
Obviously, you started
shooting the show last year.

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:11.878
You had shot a bunch of episodes
before any of us saw it.

00:00:11.878 --> 00:00:12.912 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right.

00:00:12.912 --> 00:00:15.315 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So it was not
the giant hit it is now.

00:00:15.315 --> 00:00:17.017 size:78% position:39%
Has your life changed
shooting Season 2,

00:00:17.017 --> 00:00:18.218
versus how it was Season 1?

00:00:18.218 --> 00:00:19.953 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, I mean,
I´m sitting here next to you.

00:00:19.953 --> 00:00:21.187 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That´s true.

00:00:21.187 --> 00:00:22.789
We would have had
no interest in having you here.

00:00:22.789 --> 00:00:27.727 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, no, no.
No, it was less than zero.

00:00:27.727 --> 00:00:29.596 size:78% position:39%
Yeah. No, no. It has.

00:00:29.596 --> 00:00:32.465 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, so, we had
this trailer that came out

00:00:32.465 --> 00:00:35.035
at the beginning of the series,

00:00:35.035 --> 00:00:37.003 align:start size:94% position:6%
and a bunch of people
sort of took to the trailer.

00:00:37.003 --> 00:00:38.204 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Mm-hmm.

00:00:38.204 --> 00:00:40.006 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So, we kind of knew
there was interest there,

00:00:40.006 --> 00:00:42.008 align:start size:94% position:6%
but it hadn´t aired yet,
and it was just the trailer.

00:00:42.008 --> 00:00:43.510 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was a
2-minute thing or whatever.

00:00:43.510 --> 00:00:45.245 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then the
show started gaining momentum,

00:00:45.245 --> 00:00:46.980 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it just kept
going and going and going.

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:48.748
And now we´re into Season 2.

00:00:48.748 --> 00:00:50.550 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we´ve had
this long sort of --

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:52.485 align:start size:94% position:6%
this hiatus, where everyone
has been, you know,

00:00:52.485 --> 00:00:54.554 align:start size:94% position:6%
missing the show and
wanting the show to come back.

00:00:54.554 --> 00:00:55.688
So there´s been that buildup.

00:00:55.688 --> 00:00:57.257 align:start size:94% position:6%
And now we finally
came back last week,

00:00:57.257 --> 00:00:59.826
and the ratings were better
than ever, thank goodness.

00:00:59.826 --> 00:01:01.428 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, congratulations.
-Thank you.

00:01:01.428 --> 00:01:02.996 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I will tell you --

00:01:02.996 --> 00:01:08.968
on just the scope and the reach
of your show, I did a cameo.

00:01:08.968 --> 00:01:10.804
I played myself,
a cameo in one of the episodes.

00:01:10.804 --> 00:01:12.238 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It was one of
my favorite moments.

00:01:12.238 --> 00:01:14.240 size:78% position:39%
-Thank you very much.
-Yeah. No, it was.

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:16.743
-I stumbled on you and --
Kevin and Randall fighting.

00:01:16.743 --> 00:01:19.579 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I can tell you
I got more calls and e-mails

00:01:19.579 --> 00:01:23.616 align:start size:94% position:6%
from friends about that
than I ever do about this.

00:01:23.616 --> 00:01:25.051
Like, people genuinely said,

00:01:25.051 --> 00:01:26.920 align:start size:94% position:6%
"You were so good in
´This Is Us.´

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:29.756
Are you doing anything else?"

00:01:29.756 --> 00:01:32.225
-Oh, that´s great. That´s great.
I get the same kind of thing.

00:01:32.225 --> 00:01:34.060 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, I did
a sci-fi show for a while,

00:01:34.060 --> 00:01:35.562 align:start size:94% position:6%
and there was
that fan base out there

00:01:35.562 --> 00:01:37.030
that just watches sci-fi shows.

00:01:37.030 --> 00:01:39.532
And, so, they´ll say to me --
They´ll be like, "Oh, my God!

00:01:39.532 --> 00:01:42.268
Green Arrow from ´Smallville.´
What? Did you just quit acting?"

00:01:42.268 --> 00:01:44.137 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I´m like -- I don´t even
know what to say.

00:01:44.137 --> 00:01:45.939 align:start size:94% position:6%
I´m like, "Yeah, I´m done.
I quit."

00:01:45.939 --> 00:01:47.140 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That´s better.

00:01:47.140 --> 00:01:49.375
They don´t want to see
where Green Arrow is now.

00:01:49.375 --> 00:01:51.744 align:start size:94% position:6%
"No arrows?!
You don´t have any arrows."

00:01:51.744 --> 00:01:53.279
-Yeah, exactly. Just tears.

00:01:53.279 --> 00:01:55.515 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But, so, we did
this cameo together.

00:01:55.515 --> 00:01:56.850
That was the first time we met.

00:01:56.850 --> 00:01:58.518 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was lovely to
hang out with you.

00:01:58.518 --> 00:02:00.286 align:start size:94% position:6%
But then I did not realize
we had been in a movie.

00:02:00.286 --> 00:02:01.321 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is true.

00:02:01.321 --> 00:02:03.089 align:start size:94% position:6%
We had been in
a movie before together,

00:02:03.089 --> 00:02:05.258 align:start size:94% position:6%
but we did not
have any scenes together.

00:02:05.258 --> 00:02:06.626 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was called "Spring
Breakdown."

00:02:06.626 --> 00:02:07.760 size:84% position:42%
Rachel Dratch wrote it.

00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:09.162 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we both played
love interests of her.

00:02:09.162 --> 00:02:10.463 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.

00:02:10.463 --> 00:02:11.764 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You played the hunky guy
she meets on spring break --

00:02:11.764 --> 00:02:14.868 size:84% position:42%
shirt off, looking rad.

00:02:14.868 --> 00:02:21.574
And I, her very dear friend, was
cast as her gay fiancé.

00:02:21.574 --> 00:02:24.110 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, that is me.

00:02:24.110 --> 00:02:27.046
-That´s great. That´s great.

00:02:27.046 --> 00:02:30.116 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know, when she called
and said I won a part,

00:02:30.116 --> 00:02:31.584 align:start size:94% position:6%
I just assumed
I´d be a shirt-off hunk,

00:02:31.584 --> 00:02:32.919
and she went a different way.

00:02:32.919 --> 00:02:34.521
-She went a different way.
-She went a different way.

00:02:34.521 --> 00:02:36.689 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We can´t get away
from each other.

00:02:36.689 --> 00:02:38.958 size:78% position:39%
-You got to work with
Sylvester Stallone.

00:02:38.958 --> 00:02:40.293 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-How was that?

00:02:40.293 --> 00:02:41.794
-I mean, it´s everything you

00:02:41.794 --> 00:02:43.696 align:start size:94% position:6%
could possibly imagine
times ten.

00:02:43.696 --> 00:02:47.066 align:start size:94% position:6%
It is -- I mean, I grew up
watching his movies.

00:02:47.066 --> 00:02:49.135 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yep.
-I´ve wanted to be Rocky.

00:02:49.135 --> 00:02:51.638
And, for a moment in my life, I
think I thought I was Rocky.

00:02:51.638 --> 00:02:54.374 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Sure.
-And then there he is.

00:02:54.374 --> 00:02:56.442 size:84% position:42%
I worked out with him
at the gym a few times.

00:02:56.442 --> 00:02:58.344 align:start size:94% position:6%
We go to the same gym.
How cool is that?

00:02:58.344 --> 00:03:02.615 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then Milo knows him
and sort of made a phone call.

00:03:02.615 --> 00:03:03.983 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he came.

00:03:03.983 --> 00:03:06.486 align:start size:94% position:6%
And graciously accepted
to do the role.

00:03:06.486 --> 00:03:08.121
And he´s on set, and here he is,
Sylvester Stallone.

00:03:08.121 --> 00:03:09.489 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you´re like,
"How am I supposed to work

00:03:09.489 --> 00:03:11.958
with this guy, a legend?"

00:03:11.958 --> 00:03:13.359
And he immediately disarms you.

00:03:13.359 --> 00:03:15.495 size:84% position:42%
He immediately, like,
puts everybody at ease.

00:03:15.495 --> 00:03:17.797 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he´s just, like,
the coolest guy in the world,

00:03:17.797 --> 00:03:19.632 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you´re just
having a conversation.

00:03:19.632 --> 00:03:23.169
And then he does a bang-up job,
is a wonderful actor.

00:03:23.169 --> 00:03:25.805 align:start size:94% position:6%
says a few gracious words,
tells a few jokes,

00:03:25.805 --> 00:03:26.940 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then he leaves,

00:03:26.940 --> 00:03:28.508 align:start size:94% position:6%
and as soon as he leaves,
you´re like, "Oh!"

00:03:28.508 --> 00:03:30.043 align:start size:94% position:6%
You missed him.
You were like, "Oh!

00:03:30.043 --> 00:03:31.911
Come back, Sly! Come back!"

00:03:31.911 --> 00:03:33.746 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You didn´t know
how good you had it.

00:03:33.746 --> 00:03:36.316 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He´s the real deal, man.
He´s the real -- It´s amazing.

00:03:36.316 --> 00:03:38.985
-That´s really exciting.
You have a 13-year-old daughter.

00:03:38.985 --> 00:03:42.522 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I do.
-And is she a fan of the show?

00:03:42.522 --> 00:03:43.890 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is this correct?
-Uh-huh. Yeah, yeah.

00:03:43.890 --> 00:03:45.291
-Is this exciting for you?

00:03:45.291 --> 00:03:46.526 size:81% position:41%
Is this the first time

00:03:46.526 --> 00:03:48.895
she has liked
a piece of your work like this?

00:03:48.895 --> 00:03:50.230 size:84% position:42%
-Yeah. I mean, kind of.

00:03:50.230 --> 00:03:51.464 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think she --

00:03:51.464 --> 00:03:53.800
No, not liked,
but I think it´s the first time

00:03:53.800 --> 00:03:54.867 align:start size:94% position:6%
it was, like, cool.

00:03:54.867 --> 00:03:56.769 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Sure.
´Cause you´re on a hit show

00:03:56.769 --> 00:03:58.871 align:start size:94% position:6%
that, probably, I´m assuming a
lot of her friends watch.

00:03:58.871 --> 00:04:00.640 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I mean, the parent-teacher
stuff is great.

00:04:00.640 --> 00:04:02.208 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, going to
the school is great.

00:04:02.208 --> 00:04:04.244
I´m allowed to go to
the school now, which is great.

00:04:04.244 --> 00:04:05.511 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That´s nice.

00:04:05.511 --> 00:04:07.480 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, ´cause I was on a --
Yeah, I was on a --

00:04:07.480 --> 00:04:09.616
It was a hiatus for
a year or two, and now I´m back.

00:04:09.616 --> 00:04:10.917 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Just, yeah,
wait in the parking lot,

00:04:10.917 --> 00:04:12.318
and now you can actually walk --

00:04:12.318 --> 00:04:13.920
-Yeah, she´s like, "You´re,
like, as cool as a 13-year-old."

00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:15.121 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was like,
"Well, thank you."

00:04:15.121 --> 00:04:17.123 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Whoa!
-What a compliment.

00:04:17.123 --> 00:04:19.759 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That is high praise.
-Life goals right there, man.

00:04:19.759 --> 00:04:20.793 align:start size:94% position:6%
Life goals.

00:04:20.793 --> 00:04:22.495 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You go to
a lot of Dodgers games.

00:04:22.495 --> 00:04:24.664 align:start size:94% position:6%
Congratulations
on making the postseason.

00:04:24.664 --> 00:04:26.799 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you. Thank you.
No, I bleed blue.

00:04:26.799 --> 00:04:28.334 align:start size:94% position:6%
I´m a diehard,
lifelong Dodger fan.

00:04:28.334 --> 00:04:29.602
I have been since I was a kid.

00:04:29.602 --> 00:04:31.638
My dad was a big Dodger fan
when we were growing up.

00:04:31.638 --> 00:04:33.339 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, I was the only
kid in Chicago

00:04:33.339 --> 00:04:34.707
that was, like, a Dodger fan.

00:04:34.707 --> 00:04:37.343 align:start size:94% position:6%
People would see the blue hat,
and then I´d turn around.

00:04:37.343 --> 00:04:39.178 align:start size:94% position:6%
They´d be like, "Boo!"
You know?

00:04:39.178 --> 00:04:41.614 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, so --
-Optimistic? Hopeful?

00:04:41.614 --> 00:04:42.715 align:start size:94% position:6%
How do you feel?

00:04:42.715 --> 00:04:44.083 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I´m hopeful
and optimistic every year.

00:04:44.083 --> 00:04:45.885 align:start size:94% position:6%
We stumbled a little bit going
into the playoffs,

00:04:45.885 --> 00:04:47.320 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I feel like
that builds character

00:04:47.320 --> 00:04:48.521 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I feel like --

00:04:48.521 --> 00:04:50.089
You know, they don´t need
any pep talks, obviously.

00:04:50.089 --> 00:04:51.291
They´ve got some great pitching

00:04:51.291 --> 00:04:52.859 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they´ve got
a lot of great players,

00:04:52.859 --> 00:04:54.594 align:start size:94% position:6%
a lot of energy,
and they´re good as a team

00:04:54.594 --> 00:04:56.529 align:start size:94% position:6%
when they play well together,
and they can do it.

00:04:56.529 --> 00:04:58.298 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I´m feeling good
about this year.

00:04:58.298 --> 00:05:00.900
-I think they would take that
as a pretty good pep talk.

00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:03.469 size:88% position:44%
I like that you did that
sort of back-door thing,

00:05:03.469 --> 00:05:04.737 align:start size:94% position:6%
where you said,
"This isn´t a pep talk,"

00:05:04.737 --> 00:05:05.638
but then you gave a pep talk.

00:05:05.638 --> 00:05:06.706 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That´s right.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:05:06.706 --> 00:05:07.940 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah, you can´t just
go right at it.

00:05:07.940 --> 00:05:09.609
They´d be like, "Why are
we listening to this guy?"

00:05:09.609 --> 00:05:10.543 align:start size:94% position:6%
But the way you said it, I
think they were like,

00:05:10.543 --> 00:05:12.011 size:88% position:44%
"Hey, what´s he saying?"

00:05:12.011 --> 00:05:15.048
-Don´t take any advice from me,
but this is what I would do.

00:05:15.048 --> 00:05:17.950
-Well, best of luck on that.
And congratulations on Season 2.

00:05:17.950 --> 00:05:19.452
-Thank you. Thank you so much.

